{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391352-map-of-creation","id":1391352,"title":"Map of Creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-24T17:04:26-07:00","id":1391352,"title":"Map of Creation","content":"I have attempted to make a map of creation with all the places that have had sufficiently exact locations given in any editions. I've uploaded it to Deviantart and am linking here in case anyone finds it useful or has feedback on it. <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/rorymj/art/Custom-Map-843154955?ga_submit_new=10%3A1590364163\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/rorymj/ar...0%3A1590364163</a><br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1xSzI4QKCBC6XN-fpJvRzdJBPNXpGSDJl?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Latest version</a><br /> <br /> Edit: Initial maps use Kashi's map of 3E creation in the style of previous editions' maps for a base, while newer ones use Savagejoss' river and coastline map.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":". 06-20-2020, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T05:03:14-07:00","id":1393393,"title":"","content":"Updated to move the dragon king cities (I had previously used the locations on Stephenls's map, but found that they didn't match those described in Fallen Races); add the Rainbow Palace, the Purified Ziggurat, Fatal Onyx and the Island and Jackal tribes; give Marita its' own symbol (since giving the capital of the Scavenger Lands the default city symbol wasn't really appropriate), give the Opal Court a rainbow-coloured butterfly symbol (it had previously used the Pearl Court's white butterfly symbol) and add terrestrial aspect symbols to the River Temple and Khorban Prantil symbols to represent their positions as direction-wide headquarters of the Terrestrial Bureaucracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T05:13:55-07:00","id":1393397,"title":"","content":"Very interesting, but it's unfortunately hard to read because it's too small. Unless there's some other way to zoom in further?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T12:53:43-07:00","id":1393492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391352-map-of-creation?p=1393397#post1393397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very interesting, but it's unfortunately hard to read because it's too small. Unless there's some other way to zoom in further?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you download the image you can zoom in better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T17:46:58-07:00","id":1393558,"title":"","content":"- Added Wyld locations in the intercardinal directions.<br /> - Added the Jet and Lapis courts.<br /> - Changed Ysyr symbol to the Emerald Circle symbol.<br /> <br /> I also forgot to mention in my last post that I added the Bronze Tide's neighbouring locations and the road through Marita.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":". 06-01-2020, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T18:24:57-07:00","id":1393562,"title":"","content":"A legend would be extremely useful, as the meanings of some of those symbols are not immediately obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T18:43:09-07:00","id":1393564,"title":"","content":"First: This is magnificent. Adding THAT to my map stockpile.<br /> <br /> Second: I'm with Hakkonen. A legend would be super handy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T21:13:19-07:00","id":1393578,"title":"","content":"So, I won't make a full legend for the map as it stands because early in the process of making it I decided (it seemed like a good idea at the time) to represent the capitals of all countries with full write-ups with symbols of those countries, even if I had to make up symbols for them in order to do so, with the result that there are a lot of one-off symbols floating. I'm planning to go back at some point and change the symbol scheme, but in the meantime the symbols that show up in more than one place are:<br /> <br /> White castle: human settlement<br /> White castle with broken towers: human ruins<br /> Blue castle: person-of-the-air settlement<br /> Black castle: person-of-the-sea settlement<br /> Grey cog: mountainfolk settlement<br /> Green butterfly: Fey freehold<br /> Bigger butterfly in other colour: Major fey court<br /> Orange trapezium: mixed-species dragon-king settlement<br /> Trapezium in other colour: single-species dragon-king settlement<br /> Flatter, inverted trapezium: Realm navy fleet home port<br /> Orange trapezium with broken top: dragon-king ruins<br /> Autochthonian sodality symbol: alchemical manse<br /> Silver crescent: lunar dominion<br /> Fuzzy-edged black circle: shadowland<br /> Hard-edged black circle with symbol inside: deathlord's stronghold<br /> Purple circle with silver crescent along left edge and animal inside: changing moon dominion<br /> Dawn caste symbol in saffron with symbol on lavender centre: dawn's stronghold<br /> Great house mon: great house primary centre of power<br /> Blue gate with grey frame: gate of Yu-Shan<br /> Grey gate flanked by grey pillars: divine sanctum<br /> My personal design for the seal of the guild (a light grey circle containing a design consisting of a ship, a wagon, two curved arrows forming circle and a number of small circles representing coins): guild trade post<br /> Blue circle with silver border: no-moon dominion<br /> Gold gauntlet in red circle: Cult of the Illuminated training camp<br /> Grey animal on white circle: full moon dominion<br /> Element symbol on the Caul: shrine city<br /> Plant: Bureau of Nature directional headquarters<br /> Celestial symbol with terrestrial symbol on centre: divine bureau directional headquarters<br /> Down-pointing pentagon with circular symbol in centre: Shogunate remnants independent of Realm<br /> Pentagram with dragon symbols at points: Immaculate holy site<br /> Also, if there's an area where lots of labels have a particular unusual colour it probably means all the places they label are controlled by the same state, stand-alone green text typically denotes Fae states, stand-alone silver text typically denotes lunar dominions.<br /> <br /> but as I said, there's also lots of inconsistent or one-off symbols that you'll just need to figure out what mean by their labels. I realise I should probably make things more regular.<br /> Also, at this point no location has more than one symbol, even though there are plenty of places that have more than one of those features (e.g. Chiaroscuro is, in 2E, a lunar dominion with a directional bureau headquarters). Figuring out a solution for this is a major reason I haven't yet started on a more consistent map.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":". 06-02-2020, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T02:28:26-07:00","id":1393599,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I definitely encourage you to dramatically simplify the symbols. Let me throw a few ideas at you (these are off the top of my head, and in no particular order):<ul><li>One symbol for all lunar dominions. Different symbols for Lunar castes needlessly complicates the map, and if it's important in your game, you can look it up.</li> <li>The main political divide in Creation is Realm vs. non-Realm; make the castle icon one color for actual Realm cities, a shade of the same color for Threshold (Realm tributary) settlements (dark red and bright red?), and a different color for independent settlements.</li> <li>Features like Cult of the Illuminated camps, Guild trading posts, etc. can be indicated by smaller icons next to, above, or below a settlement icon. Dynastic House mons can be represented the same way.</li> </ul><br /> Basically, simplify and standardize your iconography.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T02:08:28-07:00","id":1396136,"title":"","content":"So, I've made some of the changes that people have advised (and also some others, such as adding borders). The map now uses Savagejoss's map as a base rather than Kashi's. I decided the changes this time were big enough that I'd leave the other one where it was and upload the new one separately. Link below:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/rorymj/art/Custom-Map-Simplified-845333320\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/rorymj/ar...fied-845333320</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T03:30:12-07:00","id":1396144,"title":"","content":"Modified to add locations of major lines of the great houses. Incidentally, can anyone point me to a site that allows uploading of bigger images than Deviant Art does? The image is as big as the site allows but some of the symbols and labels are hard to make out and if I make them any bigger they won't fit into the places where there lots of things close together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T04:38:35-07:00","id":1396155,"title":"","content":"Maybe Imgur?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T19:20:03-07:00","id":1396277,"title":"","content":"By the look of it Imgur has a limit of 20MB, which is less than a sixth of the size of my current image.<br /> <br /> Updated to add locations from Time of Tumult and The Autochthonians, plus the most prominent realm primary schools and the underwater manse of Peleps Kaizoku.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T02:12:43-07:00","id":1396334,"title":"","content":"- Added Cathedral of Opal Dreams and Irian-Ves<br /> - Added locations from Dreams of the First Age as first age ruins (I took the locations from a map that says it's copyright of 'CCP hf' - I don't know if that's official or not)<br /> - Added example freeholds from the sidebar on page 33 of Compass: Wyld<br /> - Fixed appearance of Caracal River","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:12:55-07:00","id":1396460,"title":"","content":"I love this, but unfortunately the legend is far too small to read, even when I download the image. Could it be saved separately, so as to be more legible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:35:56-07:00","id":1396521,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/rorymj/art/Legend-845507405\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/rorymj/art/Legend-845507405</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:47:16-07:00","id":1396558,"title":"","content":"- Fixed nonsensical Realm border near Thorns<br /> - Changed locations of Ironfall and Fair Isle<br /> - added Realm border in North<br /> - added border for Tear Eater lands<br /> - moved Realm and Haslanti League borders near Shanarinara","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T11:53:41-07:00","id":1396705,"title":"","content":"Definitely too small to read even when downloaded. Maybe if I had it on a big TV instead of a monitor. But very much not on my Laptop at its native resolution.<br /> <br /> But even what bits I can make out are helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T11:57:15-07:00","id":1396706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391352-map-of-creation?p=1396705#post1396705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely too small to read even when downloaded. Maybe if I had it on a big TV instead of a monitor. But very much not on my Laptop at its native resolution.<br /> <br /> But even what bits I can make out are helpful!</div> </div> </div> </div>If you download you should be able to zoom in as far as you want. (At least, I could read it when I downloaded and zoomed in.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T17:08:12-07:00","id":1396756,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, why does that whole lakes region in Khirgast/Harborhead look like a shadowland?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T19:23:36-07:00","id":1396784,"title":"","content":"I thought that was supposed to be the bayou of endless regret? I wasn't confident in that guess, but the Jiara was where the bayou used to be, and the lake area was nearby and seemed kind of similar to a bayou, and the bayou had been big, and I wasn't sure where else to put it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T10:37:42-07:00","id":1396898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rj.au</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391352-map-of-creation?p=1396784#post1396784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that was supposed to be the bayou of endless regret? I wasn't confident in that guess, but the Jiara was where the bayou used to be, and the lake area was nearby and seemed kind of similar to a bayou, and the bayou had been big, and I wasn't sure where else to put it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lakes are roughly equal to the Mediterranean Sea in area (with quibbles about length, width, land area, etch). I don't think the Bayou is quite that big.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T14:53:51-07:00","id":1396949,"title":"","content":"I never got around to putting trade routes or 1E/2E locations on my map. This has reminded me to do that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Map of Third Edition Creation in a First Edition Style<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2F18ttip13xdsc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D35f3d332551385032587cde8b093e4923ed687ee\" target=\"_blank\">\u200b</a>, (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fpjil7fcr0esc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3Dcfdff833d8e8afe3e86ca27c06569cad0bb44be9\" target=\"_blank\">3E Locations Only</a>) (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fik6dit8lrlrc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D0e0c488dea6e066af00d52c6d5994592bb4d8359\" target=\"_blank\">1E, 2E, 3E Amalgam</a>)\u200b<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/kashi85\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt, where I post some Exalted stuffs.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/853-kashi","name":"Kashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar853_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T17:31:58-07:00","id":1396971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391352-map-of-creation?p=1396706#post1396706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you download you should be able to zoom in as far as you want. (At least, I could read it when I downloaded and zoomed in.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for me, it seems stuck at a certain resolution so zooming gets super pixelated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T20:00:17-07:00","id":1396998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391352-map-of-creation?p=1396971#post1396971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not for me, it seems stuck at a certain resolution so zooming gets super pixelated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you log on to DeviantArt and download it or just download the displayed image?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T05:36:37-07:00","id":1397066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391352-map-of-creation?p=1396998#post1396998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you log on to DeviantArt and download it or just download the displayed image?</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried both, same result as Dulahan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T03:56:58-07:00","id":1397260,"title":"","content":"Google Drive has been recommended to me as a site that allows hosting of larger files. A larger version of the map is now available at <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1xSzI4QKCBC6XN-fpJvRzdJBPNXpGSDJl?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folde...Jl?usp=sharing</a>. This version also adds:<br /> - symbols for states and cities identified as being among the [number] largest in their direction<br /> - symbols to distinguish the five great fair folk courts from lesser courts<br /> - the Lapis and Opal courts<br /> - Karasch<br /> - major realm primary schools, and secondary schools outside of the top 5<br /> - major lines of great houses<br /> in addition, pale green has been extended to represent grassland in general rather than just savannah, and the Bayou of Endless Regret is now a smaller area to the north of the lake region rather than the entire lake region.<br /> I'm now trying to decide whether to add symbols for homes of exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:57:50-07:00","id":1397697,"title":"","content":"- Marked Realm navy fleet home ports<br /> - Marked more sanctums of major gods<br /> - Added symbol for infernal cults<br /> - Marked homes of celestial exalted, green sun princes and terrestrial exalted families<br /> - Marked Djala lands<br /> - Changed label of scavenger lands to read 'Confederation of Rivers'<br /> - Marked faction allegiance of lunar dominions<br /> - Fixed some errors in marking of god-ruled areas<br /> - Added symbol for miscellaneous gates to other realms of existence (i.e. Palanquin, the Well of Udr and the Seal of Eight Divinities)<br /> - Marked minor outposts of the Cult of the Illuminated<br /> - Added Fatal Onyx, and moved Xu-Lak and the Opal Court<br /> - Fixed Ilo Stara being marked as abandoned, and marked it as a lunar dominion<br /> - Marked tundra in white<br /> - Added symbols for major centres of sorcery and necromancy<br /> - Marked Guild hub cities, and additional Guild-dominated locations<br /> - Marked Bronze Tide's allegiance to Sha'a Oka.<br /> - altered border of the area controlled by Saloy Hin<br /> - Labeled the Indigo Chain and marked Vajkaimal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T17:57:45-07:00","id":1397865,"title":"","content":"I realised I forgot to update the latest version link to point to Google Drive rather than Deviant Art, so I did that. I have also now updated the map to add the Rutting Pens, and to add the sorcerous and necromantic academies from the Black and White Treatises (both as centres for sorcery/necromancy and other things indicated by them, such as the presence of a lunar in Great Forks)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T03:41:36-07:00","id":1397939,"title":"","content":"Small update to mark Gethamane as having Solar exalted, per the Antagonists section of the 2E scorebook, and to make some minor modifications to borders near the Forest Witches.<br /> Things I'm considering doing now:<br /> - Adding stuff from home-brew and third party material<br /> - Marking locations of behemoths<br /> - Adding symbol for individual Terrestrial exalted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T02:11:04-07:00","id":1398561,"title":"","content":"New version:<br /> - Marks several locations of celestial-circle sorcerers I had previously missed (I have been treating celestial-circle sorcerers as automatically constituting significant sorcerous presences)<br /> - Marks Skhandhar Bhal as being a lunar dominion<br /> - Marks the car tunnels of the mountain folk<br /> - Marks underworld locations (I decided that while they aren't strictly part of creation, interaction between nearby places in the two is probably easier than interaction between distant places in the same realm, so it makes sense to put them on the same map)<br /> - Marks the locations of the few behemoths whose locations are specified precisely enough that I judged them to be worth marking<br /> - Marks locations of ancestor-cults and cults of major gods, as well as hundred-god-heresy hotspots in the blessed isle and centres of the immaculate philosophy outside the realm<br /> - Marks locations of nocturnals given in the popular fans plat, as well as as Sahmet El-Ursha from Terrifying Argent Witches (one of a number of locations from that book, but the only one I could find that had a location specified precisely enough to map)<br /> - Marked Sijian as being the only stated home both of Eternals (from the recent popular third-party supplement) and (so far) of Liminals<br /> - Marked various ruined cities mentioned in Underworld that I saw mentioned while looking for underworld locations and realised I hadn't marked<br /> - Removed border of the Shadow Fang Vanguard dominions (they didn't meet my normal standards for adding borders, namely that either the books indicate where the borders are in more detail than just the approximate location of the name would convey or there be multiple locations stated to be within the state, but for some reason I had given it a border anyway<br /> - Added Golden Leaf Canal<br /> - Marked settlements with significant fair-folk minorities<br /> <br /> Things I'm now considering doing:<br /> - Marking deployment of Realm legions<br /> - Marking houses of 2E satraps and prefects (where they differ from 3E)<br /> - Adding symbol for individual Terrestrial exalted<br /> - Adding symbol for Wyld zones<br /> - Marking the boundary of the Wyld<br /> - Marking places with batsman populations<br /> - Adding some distinction between the symbols for 'settlement of weird one-off beings' and 'human settlement'<br /> - Add symbols for lesser manses and demesnes (possibly the same symbol but with a numeral to indicate the rating?)<br /> - Expand Halta to put Kajeth at the mouth of the Rock<br /> - Mark houses of garrison commanders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":". 06-24-2020, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T03:39:10-07:00","id":1398749,"title":"","content":"- Moved roads and settlements to better align with each other and with coasts<br /> - Fixed spelling of Dehennan Mountains and made the label bigger (as it was previously smaller than that of the Silverholds<br /> - Added Wallport<br /> - Added liminals and Knights of Eternity to the key<br /> - Marked Feverfew Valley (it was previously labeled but not marked)<br /> - Fixed some of the cases of terrain spilling over the coast<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> another update, but very soon after:<br /> - Marked Memon-Darjilis, the House of Vines and the Ledaal Catala household as sorcerer-controlled","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":". 06-25-2020, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T04:09:22-07:00","id":1402038,"title":"","content":"New version:<br /> - Marks the Coral protectorates as the home of a nocturnal<br /> - Extends the scavenger lands to the former location of Farhold (per 1E Lunars)<br /> - Marks the Ice Plains as a lunar dominion (per 1E Lunars)<br /> - Separates the notabl sorcerous and necromantic presence symbols into seperate symbols for second-circle practitioners and institutions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T04:28:32-07:00","id":1402393,"title":"","content":"New version of map:<br /> - Marks necropoloi that are the largest in their direction<br /> - Marks Caul shrine cities<br /> - Adds grasslands on the Caul<br /> - Fixes places where the terrain colouring went over the coastline<br /> - Adds the Isle of Eternal Leaves and Chin Jai Ru, and no longer marks the Ragara Soras household as being on Thistlefall<br /> - Marks the informal power of Sesus in Chanos and Peleps in Sdoia, and the power Ragara has over the Daoshin Peninsula via the Minister of Renewal<br /> - Marks Peleps' power over Radimel's Seat as other/informal rather than prefectorial<br /> - Changed Radimel's Seat's name (from Sweet Radiance)<br /> - Moved most of the symbols for things at the summit of the imperial mountain from the left of the location mark to beneath it<br /> - Marked Pasiap's Shadow as not under realm control<br /> - Added Silver Pact faction affiliated dominions to the key<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Shortly after, I uploaded another new version, with:<br /> - Feng-Yi no longer marked as inhabited<br /> - Adds Malif Nganto as Lunar with home among the Lintha<br /> - No longer shows Dukantha as being in Bluehaven<br /> <br /> And a third version, this time to mark Wallport and the Travellers' Road as being under the control of Whitewall and Marama's Fell as not under the control of the Realm but surrounded by places that are","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":". 07-12-2020, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T07:37:33-07:00","id":1402598,"title":"","content":"What does the upper left symbol on Wu-Jian mean? I can't find that one in the legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T15:27:38-07:00","id":1402693,"title":"","content":"It means its satrap is a Sesus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T16:43:37-07:00","id":1402698,"title":"","content":"So it's under control of a cadet branch of House Sesus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T17:40:59-07:00","id":1402702,"title":"","content":"No, Realm satrapies have native governments in addition to the Satrap, and Wu Jian's native government is controlled by a cadet house (House Nissar) while its satrap is a Sesus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T07:12:03-07:00","id":1404235,"title":"","content":"New version:<br /> - Adds distinct symbol for non-canon locations<br /> - Adds the Weyleen Archipelago and Proto Puma Prime (I changed my mind about their locations being insufficiently specified)<br /> - Marks populations of beastfolk, god-blooded and Wyld mutans<br /> - Marks Wyld zones<br /> - Marks locations of major artefacts, artefact caches, magical material mines and artefact production centres<br /> - Marks locations of terrestrial martial arts dojos and celestial martial arts masters<br /> - Marks places with Immaculate heresies<br /> - Marks the mesa-settlement of Saman Dar-Al<br /> - Marks the homes of massive thaumaturgical organisations (per Oadenol's codex)<br /> - Marks locations of sources of essence enlightenment<br /> - Marks localised sources of sorcerous initiation<br /> - Fixes Yu-Shan Gate 16 being marked separately from the River-Temple of Anisatsis when MoEP:Siderials states that gate 16 is on the River Temple<br /> - Marks locations of dynastic estates<br /> - Marks locations of Realm legions<br /> - Marks the solar governors of Karn and Plenilune<br /> - Marks directional missions of the Immaculate Order<br /> - Marks houses of Wyld Hunt ostiaries where apparent<br /> - Marks the Lap as having a Cathack co-satrap (per The Realm)<br /> - Marks locations of shahan-yas<br /> - Marks the deep villages of the Djala<br /> - Moves Serrat, Wallport, Inahjal and Gildei in an attempt to make everything fit together better in that part and mark the Vichas principalities as part of Pneuma<br /> - Added the Winter Folk and Lions of the Snow<br /> - Added locations of individual dragon-blooded not otherwise marked<br /> - Added Voice of Storms' manse<br /> - Filled the An-Teng Middle Lands in with jungle<br /> <br /> Further changes I'm considering making:<br /> -Marking woodlands and hills separately from forests and mountains","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T22:27:41-07:00","id":1404362,"title":"","content":"- Marked places sacred to the Immaculate Order and the Incarnae<br /> - Marked places suited to geomantic engineering of greater solar demesnes<br /> <br /> Edit: another version, uploaded shortly afterwards:<br /> - Marks Eseon Forest as home to sorcerers, fair folk, forbidden gods and nameless monsters (per The Realm)<br /> - Labels the Dark Glass Lowlands<br /> <br /> and another:<br /> - Marks Pymander Seven as a celestial martial artist<br /> - moves the label on Star-of-Prose to a position where it's clearer that it's not referring to Raiton's Perch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":". 07-25-2020, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T05:05:02-07:00","id":1408886,"title":"","content":"While making these maps, I have found the base maps I've been using unsatisfactory. I have now made my own base map, and am making it available for others to use. It is in the same Google Drive folder as the other map (I intend to use my own baseman for future versions of the map, but have not yet done so).<br /> <br /> Primary features of the map I consider to be of value for a base map:<br /> - Seperate symbols for forest, grassland and tundra, plus roads and shipping lanes - basically all the feature of the official maps but without labels to obscure things (also no cities or dominion borders, as those seemed to be the start of a slippery slope that lead to adding far more detail than made for a suitable base map, and also of much less use without labels)<br /> - Terrains showed as simple, flat colours, making it easy to, for example, add lakes or islands for use in your own game<br /> <br /> Other liberties I've taken I consider worth noting:<br /> - Included borders of different types of forest from the 1e map, and volcanic mountains from the 1e and 2e maps<br /> - Included geographical features from earlier editions where there seemed to be minimal chance of their presence being actively undesirable in a game, such as the islands to the west of the Blessed Isle and the hills south of Lookshy<br /> - Moved roads and shipping lanes slightly with a view to having cities located on coasts and rivers rather than the width of the city symbols away<br /> - Marked various areas of unclear terrain either to match a neighbouring area of clearer terrain or as grassland<br /> - Marked rivers as lines (I don't know whether the rivers are meant to be amazingly wide in keeping with the larger-than-life setting, or if I'm underestimating how wide real rivers get on account of having lived near several small rivers but not near any large ones, or if the width of the rivers is exaggerated on the maps, but in any case marking them as lines isn't a stance on their actual width)<br /> - No distinction as to the height of mountains, or between mountains and hills (this is purely a matter of laziness on my part)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":". 08-18-2020, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T05:45:33-07:00","id":1408895,"title":"","content":"Is the correct one the custom map simplified.jpg ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T16:20:28-07:00","id":1409032,"title":"","content":"Custom map simplified is the old one. The base map is Base Map.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T02:18:29-07:00","id":1409097,"title":"","content":"Maybe there is a link problem because when I go to the update link you posted on your first post I'm send to <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/12aimmpdoJTehYYPGfBb3BMGtZnlG60Ck/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">this image</a>, which seems to have much less content that you describe in your subsequent posts. Maybe I've followed the wrong link, but I'm pretty sure I went to the updated page on your first post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"th